<div class="guide-styles" data-ay-injected="true" data-zaf-dynamic="article" id="guide-body" lang="en">Welcome to Wowhead's Phase 3 Best in Slot Gear list for Protection Warrior Tank in Wrath of the Lich King Classic. Gear in this guide is primarily obtained from Trial of the Crusader and Onyxia (80). This guide will list the recommended gear for your class and role, containing gear sourced from raids, dungeons, PvP, professions, BoE World drops, and reputations.<h2 class="heading-size-2" id="best-in-slot">Best in Slot Gear for Protection Warrior Tank in Phase 3</h2>
<a data-entity="zone" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/zone=4722/trial-of-the-crusader">
<span class="tinyicontxt">Trial of the Crusader</span></a> (<b>Heroic</b>) is a mixed bag when it comes to damage dealt to tanks. Half the bosses are a significant step down from the last phase, with damage output lower than even <a data-entity="zone" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/zone=3456/naxxramas">
<span class="tinyicontxt">Naxxramas</span></a> encounters. <a data-entity="npc" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/npc=34796/gormok-the-impaler">
<span class="tinyicontxt">Gormok the Impaler</span></a>, <a data-entity="npc" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/npc=34797/icehowl">
<span class="tinyicontxt">Icehowl</span></a> and <a data-entity="npc" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/npc=34564/anubarak">
<span class="tinyicontxt">Anub'arak</span></a> are heavy hitters but even they pale in comparison to <a data-entity="npc" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/npc=32871/algalon-the-observer">
<span class="tinyicontxt">Algalon the Observer</span></a> dishing out double the pain as these new Phase 3 bosses. <br/>
<br/>The Phase 3 BiS is a significant upgrade from the Phase 2 BiS, with up to 16% less damage taken on Algalon. However, most of these upgrades will feel superfluous to a tank decked out in <a data-entity="zone" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/zone=4273/ulduar">
<span class="tinyicontxt">Ulduar</span></a> gear, which increased item levels already bring the probability of dying to the assaults of any <a data-entity="zone" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/zone=4722/trial-of-the-crusader">
<span class="tinyicontxt">Trial of the Crusader</span></a> boss down to 0%. At least you won't be responsible for any wipe. In the quest for the coveted ilvl 272 capes, it's better to be safe than sorry!<ul>
<li class="fa fa-frown-o">
<div data-markup-content-target="1">Unfortunately, Blizzard has decided to cancel the iconic <a href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/guide/building-a-block-gear-set">Block Sets</a> of original WotLK by changing the damage formula for the <a data-entity="npc" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/npc=34607/nerubian-burrower">
<span class="tinyicontxt">Nerubian Burrower</span></a>'s <a class="icontiny" data-entity="spell" data-entity-has-icon="true" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/spell=67721/expose-weakness">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/ability_criticalstrike.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Expose Weakness</span></a> debuff. The mini-game of building your "unhittable" gear set for this encounter is out. Instead, you will use your regular mitigation set, with a few swaps if you have spare items to enchant with Nature Resistance.</div></li></ul>
<i>Keep in mind that gearing your <span class="c1">Protection</span> <a class="icontiny c1" data-entity="class" data-game="wow" data-type="class" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/warrior">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/class_warrior.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Warrior</span></a> highly depends on your raiding environment. While I may recommend mostly defensive gear sets that will fit the majority of players, only you can know what kind of threat is needed in your raid. If your guild requires a <i>higher threat ceiling</i> to withstand the pressure from high-performing damage dealers, then feel free to mix in threat-oriented items to find the <b>balance</b> between threat and survival that works best for <i>your</i> group. But first, make sure your rotation is on point with this <a href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/guide/classes/warrior/protection/tank-rotation-cooldowns-abilities-pve">Rotation and Cooldowns guide</a>!</i>
<ul>
<li class="fa fa-question">
<div data-markup-content-target="1">
<b>How good is the <a href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item-set=-200/triumphant-wrynns-plate">Protection Warrior Tier 9 set</a>?</b></div></li>
<ul>
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">2 pieces: <a href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/spell=67269">Decreases the cooldown on your Taunt ability by 2 sec and increases the damage done by your Devastate ability by 5%.</a></div></li>
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">4 pieces: <a href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/spell=67273">Decreases the cooldown on your Shield Block ability by 10 sec.</a></div></li></ul>
<li class="fa fa-arrow-right">
<div data-markup-content-target="1">Similarly to the previous <a href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/spell=64933">T8 bonus</a>, the 2-piece bonus of Tier 9 is a decent damage increase to <a class="icontiny" data-entity="spell" data-entity-has-icon="true" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/spell=47498/devastate">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_sword_11.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Devastate</span></a>, which brings additional threat all the while still wearing mitigation-focused items. The <a href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item=48430">helm</a> and <a href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item=48454">shoulders</a> are BiS both in their ilvl 245 and 258 versions so this set bonus is the cherry on top.<br/>
<br/>The <a href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/spell=67273">4-piece bonus</a> reduces the cooldown of <a class="icontiny" data-entity="spell" data-entity-has-icon="true" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/spell=2565/shield-block">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/ability_defend.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Shield Block</span></a> down to 30 seconds when paired with the mandatory <a class="icontiny" data-entity="spell" data-entity-has-icon="true" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/spell=29599/shield-mastery">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/ability_warrior_shieldmastery.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Shield Mastery</span></a> talent, which is a significant increase in damage mitigation for most encounters, and a much better bonus than the previous set. While the rest of the ilvl 245 T9 items aren't the best individually, this set bonus makes running 4/<wbr/>5 T9 well worth it.</div></li></ul>
<ul>
<li class="fa fa-question">
<div data-markup-content-target="1">
<b>How important is the ilvl 258 T9 set for a <span class="c1">Protection</span> <a class="icontiny c1" data-entity="class" data-game="wow" data-type="class" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/warrior">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/class_warrior.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Warrior</span></a>?</b></div></li>
<li class="fa fa-arrow-right">
<div data-markup-content-target="1">The upgrade from <b>4x ilvl 245 T9</b> to <b>4x ilvl 258 T9</b> amounts to an additional <b>4.8% damage reduction</b> on average for a <span class="c1">Protection</span> <a class="icontiny c1" data-entity="class" data-game="wow" data-type="class" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/warrior">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/class_warrior.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Warrior</span></a>. In all honesty, this additional damage reduction is entirely overkill given the low threat of <a data-entity="zone" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/zone=4722/trial-of-the-crusader">
<span class="tinyicontxt">Trial of the Crusader</span></a> bosses, so one could say <span class="c1">Protection</span> <a class="icontiny c1" data-entity="class" data-game="wow" data-type="class" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/warrior">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/class_warrior.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Warrior</span></a> is a low-priority target for these limited Regalia tokens. Then again, the <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item=47558/regalia-of-the-grand-protector">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_chest_chain_03.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Regalia of the Grand Protector</span></a> is only shared with <a class="icontiny c1" data-entity="class" data-game="wow" data-type="class" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/warrior">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/class_warrior.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Warrior</span></a>
<span class="c1">s</span>, <a class="icontiny c3" data-entity="class" data-game="wow" data-type="class" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/hunter">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/class_hunter.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Hunter</span></a>
<span class="c3">s</span> and <a class="icontiny c7" data-entity="class" data-game="wow" data-type="class" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/shaman">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/class_shaman.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Shaman</span></a>
<span class="c7">s</span>, all classes with low representation in raids so the waiting list may be quite short.<br/>
<b>The <span class="c1">Protection</span> <a class="icontiny c1" data-entity="class" data-game="wow" data-type="class" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/warrior">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/class_warrior.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Warrior</span></a> uses the same 4 parts T9 items in both ilvl 245 or ilvl 258, so they can be easily substituted in the BiS sets</b>.</div></li></ul>
