<h3 class="heading-size-3" id="feet">Feet for Protection Warrior Tank in Phase 3</h3>Boots in Phase 3 are pretty clear cut: you have a full-on mitigation item in the form of <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item=47003/dawnbreaker-greaves">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_boots_plate_06.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Dawnbreaker Greaves</span></a>, and you have a big hit rating alternative with <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item=47952/sabatons-of-the-lingering-vortex">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_boots_plate_06.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Sabatons of the Lingering Vortex</span></a> that can be swapped in when you need to make a push towards hit cap, against <a data-entity="npc" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/npc=34564/anubarak">
<span class="tinyicontxt">Anub'arak</span></a> for example. You will want both options to cover your basis, with different gems and enchants for versatility.<br/>
<br/>
