<h3 class="heading-size-3" id="rings">Rings for Protection Warrior Tank in Phase 3</h3>While the ring slot was a popular source of hit or expertise rating to round up your gear in previous phases, in Phase 3 all the tank rings are essentially mitigation-only rings. This is a design that unfortunately affects all the tank items for this phase, with only 2 major pieces coming with hit rating. <br/>
<br/>As the only ilvl 258 tank ring, <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item=47157/signet-of-the-traitor-king">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_jewelry_ring_57.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Signet of the Traitor King</span></a> is a default BiS due to its increased item budget and an ideal mitigation ring with its choice of secondary stats. <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item=47955/loop-of-the-twin-valkyr">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_jewelry_ring_59.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Loop of the Twin Val'kyr</span></a> is the second best ring for pure mitigation against physical damage thanks to its bonus armor.<br/>
<a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item=45471/fates-clutch">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_jewelry_ring_69.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Fate's Clutch</span></a> from <a data-entity="zone" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/zone=4273/ulduar">
<span class="tinyicontxt">Ulduar</span></a> is still an excellent choice for Phase 3, with expertise rating in place of a third mitigation roll and higher item budget than the rest of the options for this phase. <br/>
<br/>If your luck with rings has been terrible for quite some time, <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item=47731/clutch-of-fortification">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_jewelry_ring_50naxxramas.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Clutch of Fortification</span></a> is a decent option you can buy with your spare <a class="icontiny q1" data-entity="currency" data-game="wow" data-type="currency" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/currency=301/emblem-of-triumph">
<span>
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/spell_holy_summonchampion.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Emblem of Triumph</span></span></a> a few weeks into Phase 3. And so is <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item=45247/signet-of-the-earthshaker">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_jewelry_ring_74.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Signet of the Earthshaker</span></a> that you should be able to find at the Auction House as a catch-up ring. <br/>
<br/>
<a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item=49489/signified-ring-of-binding">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_jewelry_ring_13.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Signified Ring of Binding</span></a> is a niche item but definitely worth grabbing because it may come in handy for a couple encounters throughout the rest of WotLK. It comes with a mitigation score similar to <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item=47955/loop-of-the-twin-valkyr">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_jewelry_ring_59.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Loop of the Twin Val'kyr</span></a> or <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item=45247/signet-of-the-earthshaker">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_jewelry_ring_74.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Signet of the Earthshaker</span></a> but with zero threat due to the absence of strength or block value. However, it's a unique ring providing magic resistances as a bonus to an already high EHP increase. In Phase 3 specifically, it can be swapped in as a Nature Resistance piece in your <a data-entity="npc" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/npc=34564/anubarak">
<span class="tinyicontxt">Anub'arak</span></a> set. In the future, it may be used again to fight <a data-entity="npc" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/npc=36853/sindragosa">
<span class="tinyicontxt">Sindragosa</span></a>.<br/>
<br/>
