<h3 class="heading-size-3" id="trinkets">Trinkets for Protection Warrior Tank in Phase 3</h3>Phase 3 introduces even more tank trinkets than last phase and some interesting variety, although not all of them are upgrades. <br/>
<br/>
<a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item=47088/satrinas-impeding-scarab">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_scarab_crystal.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Satrina's Impeding Scarab</span></a> is the best trinket for Phase 3, with the highest item level, stamina amount, and a decent <a href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/spell=67753">on-use effect</a> increasing your maximum health by 5186 for 15 seconds, or roughly +10%. It pairs well with other cooldowns, especially against <a data-entity="npc" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/npc=32871/algalon-the-observer">
<span class="tinyicontxt">Algalon the Observer</span></a> or in anticipation of a burst window such as <a data-entity="npc" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/npc=34564/anubarak">
<span class="tinyicontxt">Anub'arak</span></a>'s <a class="icontiny" data-entity="spell" data-entity-has-icon="true" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/spell=66012/freezing-slash">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/spell_frost_frostblast.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Freezing Slash</span></a> removing all avoidance. Overall, it's the most versatile trinket against physical, magical or true damage and a trinket you might never unequip for the phase. <br/>The non-heroic <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item=47080/satrinas-impeding-scarab">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_scarab_crystal.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Satrina's Impeding Scarab</span></a> is the next best pick in that category but you can only equip one, and <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item=45158/heart-of-iron">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_spiritshard_01.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Heart of Iron</span></a> is a distant third against mixed or heavy magical damage.<br/>
<br/>The <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item=47735/glyph-of-indomitability">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_spiritshard_01.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Glyph of Indomitability</span></a> is a sleeper OP trinket. Most players would ignore it because it has no stam, but its enormous bonus armor actually makes for an excellent trinket to mitigate the damage taken and death probability against heavy physical hitters such as <a data-entity="npc" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/npc=32871/algalon-the-observer">
<span class="tinyicontxt">Algalon the Observer</span></a>, <a data-entity="npc" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/npc=34797/icehowl">
<span class="tinyicontxt">Icehowl</span></a> or <a data-entity="npc" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/npc=34564/anubarak">
<span class="tinyicontxt">Anub'arak</span></a>. On the other hand, it will prove rather weak against <a data-entity="npc" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/npc=34796/gormok-the-impaler">
<span class="tinyicontxt">Gormok the Impaler</span></a>, <a data-entity="npc" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/npc=34780/lord-jaraxxus">
<span class="tinyicontxt">Lord Jaraxxus</span></a> or <a href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/npc=34497">Twin Val'kyr</a> so it's not the "equip and forget" kind of trinket. Its main downside is that it costs quite a lot of <a class="icontiny q1" data-entity="currency" data-game="wow" data-type="currency" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/currency=301/emblem-of-triumph">
<span>
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/spell_holy_summonchampion.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Emblem of Triumph</span></span></a> and you will only be able to purchase it after you acquired most of your <a href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item-set=-162">ilvl 245 T9</a>.<br/>
<br/>Do not let the ilvl 200 of <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item=47216/the-black-heart">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_misc_gem_bloodstone_02.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">The Black Heart</span></a> deceive you because this trinket punches way above its item level would indicate. The +126 stamina, while good for a dungeon trinket, is not impressive compared to <a data-entity="zone" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/zone=4273/ulduar">
<span class="tinyicontxt">Ulduar</span></a> options. However, the <a href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/spell=67653">armor proc</a> is pretty insane and puts this ilvl 200 item neck and neck with <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item=45158/heart-of-iron">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_spiritshard_01.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Heart of Iron</span></a> or <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item=46021/royal-seal-of-king-llane">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_crown_13.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Royal Seal of King Llane</span></a> when it comes to reducing sustained physical damage. That being said, the ability to control when to increase your survivability with on-use trinkets can't be ignored and will often come up ahead.<br/>
<br/>Personally, I'm not the kind of tank to bet on avoidance trinkets. But if you've always dreamed of living the <i>vanilla "Blood Talisman Tank" fantasy</i>, as we call it, Phase 3 is the only time you won't be mocked for wearing the <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item=49487/purified-onyxia-blood-talisman">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/spell_shadow_lifedrain.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Purified Onyxia Blood Talisman</span></a>. Seriously though, it's the worst trinket in this list so don't do it. And <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item=47949/fervor-of-the-frostborn">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_jewelry_talisman_02.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Fervor of the Frostborn</span></a> is worse.<div class="pad"></div>
