<h3 class="heading-size-3" id="shield">Shields for Protection Warrior Tank in Phase 3</h3>The <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item=45587/bulwark-of-algalon">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_shield_67.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Bulwark of Algalon</span></a> remains the best shield in Phase 3 for damage mitigation, while <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item=46964/crystal-plated-vanguard">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_shield_68.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Crystal Plated Vanguard</span></a> is ever so slightly better for threat, despite a deceptively large amount of block value. This is due to the aggressive diminishing returns on block value past the 1960 soft-cap, attained mostly because of the abundance of shield block value on T9 items that can't be substituted.<br/>Overall, there is no clear winner between these two items with similar item budgets. Unless you can't wait to never see that weird face on the <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item=45587/bulwark-of-algalon">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_shield_67.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Bulwark of Algalon</span></a>, then that's an easy choice.<br/>
<br/>
<a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item=45877/the-boreal-guard">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_shield_66.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">The Boreal Guard</span></a> remains competitive with these two as far as mitigation goes thanks to its 2 gem sockets, making it the highest stamina shield of the bunch in spite of the larger item level difference. It's a strong choice against heavy magic or true damage, such as <a data-entity="npc" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/npc=34796/gormok-the-impaler">
<span class="tinyicontxt">Gormok the Impaler</span></a>. But this time, the threat deficit is substantial so it's easy to position it as a 3rd pick. <br/>
<a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item=47978/bulwark-of-the-royal-guard">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_shield_68.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Bulwark of the Royal Guard</span></a> and <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item=46963/crystal-plated-vanguard">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_shield_68.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Crystal Plated Vanguard</span></a>, on the other hand, are terrible. They don't have the increased item level of the 258 shield to make up for their low-value SBV and, as a result, perform way worse than <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item=45877/the-boreal-guard">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_shield_66.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">The Boreal Guard</span></a>.<br/>
<br/>The <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item=45450/northern-barrier">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_shield_66.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Northern Barrier</span></a> is still technically the best shield for threat, with hit and expertise ratings that tend to be missing from tank items in this phase compared to the previous one. However, this small threat increase comes at a substantial cost in damage taken and death probability so I don't recommend it, especially in P3 when a wipe means no 272 cape for that week. <br/>
<br/>
